# Repos the hub suite needs checked out BESIDE it on the CI venue.
#
# Declaring a sibling here is what makes its cross-repo guards actually run. An
# UNdeclared sibling is not a neutral omission: every guard written against it
# resolves with existsSync, calls this.skip(), and the gate still prints PASS,
# so the run reports green having exercised none of them. Measured 2026-08-12,
# that gap was 1 guard here (a venue without xchain-vm ran 3723 passing / 5
# pending where a full local checkout runs 3724 / 4). See
# test/unit/sibling-coverage.test.js, which reports the surface this file leaves
# uncovered; the same gap applies to a sibling that is declared but missing.
#
# ci-dispatch.sh ships each of these at its origin/master (falling back to local
# HEAD) and REFUSES the push if one is not a checkout beside this repo, so a
# declared sibling can never be silently absent.

# Consensus-primitive conformance (quorum, equivocation header, attestation
# round) and the canonical constant map.
xchain-documentation
# The equivocation-header twin and the oracle band constant mirror.
xchain-explorer
# Attestation-relay, cross-chain-call, price-activation and coin-guard twins.
xchain-indexer
# The canonical equivocation-checkpoint twin and the oracle band constant mirror.
xchain-sdk
# The chain-registry snapshot guard.
xchain-wallet
# The oracle band constant mirror: PRICE_MAX, ORACLE_DEVIATION_THRESHOLD.
xchain-vm
